# Attacking Karn, the trigger's X damage goes to the planeswalker Myr Battlesphere is attacking, not to the player
# who controls it ("the player or planeswalker it's attacking"): Karn drops from 5 to 2 loyalty before combat damage,
# and Bot2 stays at 20.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Sol Ring
Black Lotus
Plains
Myr Battlesphere
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Sol Ring
Black Lotus
Karn, Scion of Urza
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Myr Battlesphere.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Karn, Scion of Urza.Cast
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Myr Battlesphere > Bot2.Battlefield.Karn, Scion of Urza)
Bot1.Choose(Myr Token#1; Myr Token#2; Myr Token#3)
? Bot2.Battlefield.Karn, Scion of Urza.Counters.Loyalty = 2
? Bot2.Life = 20
[Bot1.Main2]
[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot2.Graveyard = Karn, Scion of Urza
